Thinking: We need to answer using the skill. Explain missing tileSize:256, CORS, maybe attribution, minzoom/maxzoom optional. Also need to add source to map and layer. Provide full example. Also mention need to add raster layer with appropriate beforeId to avoid covering labels. Provide steps.

Below is a quick “check‑list” for the OSM raster tiles you are trying to add.  
Everything you have already written is syntactically valid, but **two small pieces are almost always required** for the tiles to appear exactly as you expect:

| What you have | What is still needed (and why) |
|---------------|--------------------------------|
| ```js { type: 'raster', tiles: ['https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png'] }``` | **`tileSize: 256`** – OSM serves 256 px tiles, while MapLibre’s raster source defaults to 512 px. Without it the imagery will look “zoomed out” (one zoom‑level off) and may appear blank at high zooms. |
|               | **`attribution` (optional but recommended)** – OSM’s licence requires you to show attribution. It does not affect rendering, but it avoids a licence‑violation warning in the console. |
|               | **CORS** – The OSM tile server already sends `Access‑Control-Allow-Origin: *`, so you’re fine here, but if you ever point at a self‑hosted raster you must make sure the server sends the header. |
|               | **A raster layer that uses the source** – Adding the source alone does nothing; you need a `map.addLayer()` call (or a layer entry in the style JSON). |
|               | **Layer order** – If you add the raster layer after the style’s `symbol` layers, it will cover the street‑name labels. Insert it **below the first symbol layer** (or any other layer you want to stay on top). |

---

## Minimal, working example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>OSM raster tiles in MapLibre</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; height:100%; }
    #map { width:100%; height:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<script>
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      // Minimal style – just a background and the OSM raster source we’ll add later
      sources: {
        // placeholder – we’ll add the real source with `addSource` below
      },
      layers: [
        { id: 'background', type: 'background', paint: { 'background-color': '#e0e0e0' } }
      ]
    },
    center: [0, 0],
    zoom: 2
  });

  map.on('load', () => {
    // 1️⃣ Add the raster source (note tileSize: 256)
    map.addSource('osm-raster', {
      type: 'raster',
      tiles: ['https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png'],
      tileSize: 256,
      // optional but polite
      attribution: '&copy; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors'
    });

    // 2️⃣ Find the first symbol layer (usually a label layer) so we can insert below it
    const firstSymbolId = map.getStyle().layers.find(l => l.type === 'symbol')?.id;

    // 3️⃣ Add the raster layer, inserting it *before* the first symbol layer
    map.addLayer(
      {
        id: 'osm-raster-layer',
        type: 'raster',
        source: 'osm-raster',
        paint: {}
      },
      firstSymbolId   // ← second argument = insert below this layer
    );
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What each line does

| Line | Reason |
|------|--------|
| `tileSize: 256` | Matches OSM’s 256 px tiles; otherwise the map would look half‑zoomed out. |
| `attribution` | Satisfies OSM’s licence; also shows up in the map’s UI if you enable `map.showTileBoundaries` or a custom control. |
| `firstSymbolId` logic | Guarantees the raster layer is added **under** the label (`symbol`) layers, so street names stay visible. |
| `addLayer(..., firstSymbolId)` | The second argument to `addLayer` is the *id of the layer that should stay on top*. By passing the first symbol layer’s id we insert the raster just beneath it. |

---

## Quick checklist you can run in the browser console

If you already have a map instance (`map`) and you want to verify that everything is wired correctly, paste the following:

```js
// 1. Source exists?
console.log('osm-raster source?', map.getSource('osm-raster'));

// 2. Tile size?
console.log('tileSize:', map.getSource('osm-raster').tileSize);

// 3. Layer exists?
console.log('osm-raster-layer?', map.getLayer('osm-raster-layer'));

// 4. Is it below a symbol layer?
const layer = map.getLayer('osm-raster-layer');
const layers = map.getStyle().layers;
const idx = layers.findIndex(l => l.id === layer.id);
const below = layers.slice(0, idx).some(l => l.type === 'symbol');
console.log('raster is below a symbol layer?', below);
```

All three `true` values mean the raster should be visible and labels should still show.

---

## Common “gotchas” you might still run into

| Symptom | Likely cause (and fix) |
|---------|------------------------|
| **Map is blank, network tab shows 200s** | You added the source but never added a layer that uses it. Add `addLayer` as shown above. |
| **Tiles appear but are shifted/zoomed** | `tileSize` is still the default 512. Set it to 256. |
| **Labels disappear** | Raster layer was added **after** the symbol layers. Insert it before the first symbol layer (or any other layer you want on top). |
| **CORS error** | Not a problem with `tile.openstreetmap.org` (it sends `*`), but if you switch to a self‑hosted raster you must configure the server to send `Access‑Control-Allow-Origin: *` (or your domain). |
| **No attribution shown** | The style you built may not have a built‑in attribution control. Add one manually: `map.addControl(new maplibregl.AttributionControl({compact: true}));` |

---

### TL;DR – What you need to add

```js
map.addSource('osm-raster', {
  type: 'raster',
  tiles: ['https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png'],
  tileSize: 256,                     // ← required for OSM tiles
  attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors' // optional but recommended
});

const firstSymbol = map.getStyle().layers.find(l => l.type === 'symbol')?.id;
map.addLayer(
  { id: 'osm-raster-layer', type: 'raster', source: 'osm-raster' },
  firstSymbol                         // ← insert below labels
);
```

Add those two lines (source + layer) after the map’s `load` event, and you’ll see the OSM raster basemap with the default MapLibre labels still on top. Happy mapping!
